# 🧬 NCBI Nucleotide Sequences Retrieval

This directory contains manually retrieved NCBI Nucleotide sequence datasets organized into dedicated subfolders for downstream computational analysis and parsing.

---

## 📂 Directory Structure

```text
Nucleotide_Sequences/
├── M13241.1/         # Mouse GAPDH gene fragment data
├── NC_000913.3/      # E. coli K-12 MG1655 complete genome data
├── NC_045512.2/      # SARS-CoV-2 Wuhan-Hu-1 complete genome data
├── NM_000518.5/      # Human Hemoglobin Subunit Beta (HBB) mRNA data
└── NM_007294.4/      # Human BRCA1 DNA repair associated mRNA data

---

## 🔬 Dataset Details

Each accession folder contains manually downloaded sequence files (FASTA / GenBank formats) representing diverse biological targets:

| Accession Folder | Organism | Gene / Target | Record Type | Sequence Size |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **`M13241.1`** | *Mus musculus* | GAPDH (Housekeeping control) | Gene Fragment | ~1,232 bp |
| **`NC_000913.3`** | *Escherichia coli* K-12 | Complete Chromosome | Bacterial Genome | ~4.64 Mb |
| **`NC_045512.2`** | *SARS-CoV-2* | Wuhan-Hu-1 Reference Genome | Viral Genome | ~29,903 bp |
| **`NM_000518.5`** | *Homo sapiens* | Hemoglobin Subunit Beta (**HBB**) | Human mRNA | ~628 bp |
| **`NM_007294.4`** | *Homo sapiens* | BRCA1 DNA Repair Associated (**BRCA1**) | Human mRNA | ~7,224 bp |

---

## 🛠️ Usage & Purpose

* **Offline Parsing:** Allows local processing of FASTA/GenBank headers, sequence records, and feature tables without reliance on live NCBI Entrez API queries.
* **Comparative Analysis:** Provides model datasets spanning viral, bacterial, mouse, and human genomic targets for sequence alignment, GC-content computation, and ORF prediction workflows.

